---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<section id="published">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Published docs</p>
    <h2>Publish docs without leaking your code.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Public pages can't carry internal paths or copied source, and they still need to be checked. Store the link outside the text: readers see clean prose, CI still verifies both the sentence and the code.</p>
    <figure>
      <div class="scroll"><img src={`${base}assets/published-docs.svg`} alt="Diagram: the public page shows only prose; the link from guide.md line 12 to validate_payment lives in the seal file; check verifies the sentence and the private code" width="960" height="300" loading="lazy"></div>
    </figure>
    <div class="two">
      <div class="card"><h3><code>publico</code>: private code</h3><p>No anchors, no internal paths, no copied code. Bind claims with <code>dockeeper link guide.md:12 src/payments.py#validate_payment</code>.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3><code>publicado</code>: public code</h3><p>Anchors allowed (hidden ones read best). Copying three or more lines of source is flagged with the file it came from.</p></div>
    </div>
    <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/publicado.py#IndiceCopias dockeeper/motor.py#vincular -->
  </div>
</section>
